      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is a basis for these concerns, as facial recognition technology has shown instances of racial bias and unequal error rates when identifying people of color or women. A study by MIT found that Amazon's Rekognition facial recognition system made more errors with darker-skinned women than lighter-skinned men. These worries are valid, and some cities, like San Francisco, have banned the use of facial recognition in public spaces due to these concerns. Others, like New York City, are addressing these issues through implemented regulations.",
